   "title": "Tailored for this setup",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "**Upscale, FLUX 3 Klein (creative)**\n\nEnlarges the image, then Klein repaints it lightly while also *looking at the original* (as `<ref_image_0>`), so layout and identity hold while new detail appears.\n\n**All settings are in the groups on the left** (Main settings, Fine-tuning); each title says what it does. The nodes they feed show the same values greyed out: nothing to change there.\n\n- **Scale factor**: output = original size x factor, rounded down to a multiple of 16 px (at most 15 px trimmed from the edges, aspect kept). *Load Image* shows the original size under the preview; *Output size* shows the result during the run. Klein handles up to about 4 MP comfortably on 12 GB (a 1 MP image at 2x); for bigger, run SeedVR2 on the result.\n- **Strength**: 0.25 subtle, **0.35 default**, 0.45-0.5 strong (starts to change things).\n- **Extra references** (keep a face or object from drifting): enable *Reference 2* / *Reference 3* (select, Ctrl+B), load e.g. a clean close-up of the face, and add a sentence to the prompt such as *\"The person looks exactly like <ref_image_1>: same face, eyes and skin.\"* Each reference costs time and memory.\n- **Prompt**: name the detail you want (\"visible skin pores, sharp fabric weave\").\n- Same seed + lower strength = safer. Output: `output/upscale/`"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "**Upscale, FLUX 3 Klein (creative)**\n\nEnlarges the image, then Klein repaints it lightly while also *looking at the original* (as `<ref_image_0>`), so layout and identity hold while new detail appears.\n\n**All settings are in the groups on the left** (Main settings, Fine-tuning); each title says what it does. The nodes they feed show the same values greyed out: nothing to change there.\n\n- **Scale factor**: output = original size x factor, rounded down to a multiple of 16 px (at most 15 px trimmed from the edges, aspect kept). *Load Image* shows the original size under the preview; *Output size* shows the result during the run. Klein handles up to about 4 MP comfortably on 12 GB (a 1 MP image at 2x); for bigger, run SeedVR2 on the result.\n- **Strength**: 0.25 subtle, **0.35 default**, 0.45-0.5 strong (starts to change things).\n- **Extra references** (keep a face or object from drifting): enable *Reference 2* / *Reference 3* (select, Ctrl+B), load e.g. a clean close-up of the face, and add a sentence to the prompt such as *\"The person looks exactly like <ref_image_1>: same face, eyes and skin.\"* Each reference costs time and memory.\n- **Prompt**: name the detail you want (\"visible skin pores, sharp fabric weave\").\n- Same seed + lower strength = safer. Output: `output/upscale/`"
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
